From c58845b3cec73211c40d43d8131ca21a3809e7fd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 22:40:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Ask Bahn: an assistant that computes its answers instead
 of composing them
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

You asked for an assistant like the one on aws.amazon.com. Before building the
box, I checked what could be behind it: server/_core/llm.ts exists, points at
a scaffold URL, needs an OPENAI_API_KEY that is not set, and is called by no
route — and the client reads data.json and localStorage and never asks the
server anything. A chat widget wired to that would spin forever, and one that
answered anyway would be inventing figures about 18,172 review rows. That is
the single defect class this project has spent its whole life removing, so it
is not what got built.

Ask Bahn answers from the data, deterministically. Fourteen skills, one per
question people actually ask this site: what is critical, what is overdue, how
old is the backlog, who is carrying the load, which checks have no Prüfer,
what is blocked, how does one Gewerk stand, what is happening at one station,
what changed, how trustworthy are the numbers, who to contact, where to go.
Every figure is computed on the spot by the same functions the Dashboard and
the Gewerk tabs use — ask it about EEA and it says 814, because /bvb-eea says
814 — and every answer carries its derivation and a link to the screen where
it can be checked. It cannot hallucinate a number because it never writes one;
it only reports what a query returned.

Understanding is German folding plus keyword scoring plus entity extraction
against the real vocabularies: a Gewerk must be one of the fourteen, a station
must be a station on file, a Projektnummer must exist. "Wie steht Vermessng"
resolves; "Wie steht QQQ" does not, and says so. Keywords match on word
boundaries after "in" inside "sind" scored a data-quality question as a
station question.

When it does not understand it says so and lists what it can do. It never
produces a sentence it cannot support — a test asserts that a question about
a 2027 budget yields no budget figure.

AgentBackend is the seam for a model, when there is one. Its contract is
deliberately narrow: a backend may choose the skill and rephrase the sentence.
It is never given the ability to supply a fact, because in a company where a
wrong figure moves a delivery date, the part that must not be probabilistic is
the arithmetic.

The panel is an <aside>, not a role="dialog": it is non-modal, does not trap
focus, and Escape closes it — announcing it as a dialog would promise a modal
contract it does not keep. It closes on navigation, whoever navigated, after
the first version left itself sitting over the page it had just sent the
reader to.
