From ce9aa484a765caf5f1b1da31a290f1f3d996a301 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 22:40:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] the relief becomes an instrument: grab it, spin it, zoom
 it, click through it
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Height already carried the value; nothing could be done with it. Now the
whole camera is in the reader's hands — drag to orbit, wheel or pinch to zoom,
click a tile to land on the rows behind it — without giving up the one thing
this panel promises, that the number is always readable from the tile rather
than inferred from the perspective.

Pointer events rather than mouse events, so mouse, trackpad, pen and touch are
one code path.

The capture is the part that mattered. Capturing on pointerdown retargets the
whole sequence to the stage, and the browser then never produces a click on
the tile that was pressed — so teaching the panel to rotate silently made
every tile unclickable. The capture is taken only once the pointer has
travelled five pixels, which is the point where the gesture stops being a
click and becomes a drag; and a drag that ends over a tile has its click
swallowed, so releasing the mouse does not also open something.

Every tile is a button that goes somewhere: the red block on the EEA row lands
on /bvb-eea?q=abgelehnt, which is the question the shape provoked. A tile with
nothing behind it is disabled rather than hidden, because an empty lane is
information.

Keyboard drives the same camera — arrows orbit, +/- zoom, Home recentres — and
the stage is focusable with a name that says so. The tilt stops at 78° rather
than 90°, because past that the tiles are edge-on and the printed numbers
disappear. Coarse pointers get 44px tiles. Transitions are dropped while a
hand is on it, so the camera cannot lag behind the hand.

The UI audit learned one narrow thing: an element carrying `data-overlay`
declares itself a floating layer, so content beneath an opaque overlay is not
reported as text painted on text. position:absolute stays audited, because
that is what the map's legend-covering card was.

Gates: tsc clean, biome unchanged at 72 pre-existing warnings, 255 unit tests
(20 new), build clean, e2e 81/81 (9 new), check-ui clean across 6 routes x 16
scenarios x 3 viewports x 4 theme combinations, stress 8/8.
